ealth","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both required IPv4 hardening outcomes are fully satisfied. Direct observations show the settings applied to every present interface and the default template, persisted in a root-owned configuration file, and recovered after node1 rebooted. Restart evidence includes pre-restart health and boot identity, reboot scheduling and observed unavailability, a different post-restart identity, and recovered sysctl, interface, route, and connectivity state.","limitations":["The generic failed-services lifecycle probe was unsupported on Alpine, although the relevant OpenRC sysctl service was directly shown healthy before and after reboot.","The connectivity check after reboot pinged node1's own managed address rather than an external peer; recovered remote command execution, interface state, and routes nevertheless provide coherent recovery evidence."]}
